  "summary": "An uncommon resident and summer visitor. Resident birds are dark grey above with closely barred underparts. Visiting birds are whiter and lightly spotted. The immature is lightly streaked. The crown is black, and the sideburns are broader than a Lanner’s. In flight it looks sharper-winged than a Lanner, though less so than a Eurasian Hobby. Newman does not describe the voice. Because the page names both residents and summer visitors, status and months were left unset. The Kemp code RB was left unchanged.",
